clearcote: one persona-activation predicate (PersonaActive) for every persona surface.

Persona gates were per patch and most tested the seed switch only, so an imported capture
(--fingerprint-profile) applied to fonts and WebGL strings but not to screen, DPR, pointer, cores,
memory or voices; cores, heap limit and audio latency read the persona in EVERY mode (a bare launch
claimed a persona core count next to host memory); and the UA-CH full version was a second,
independent draw (raw seed text parsed as int, modulo a table) that could disagree with the
persona's own version.

PersonaActive() = --fingerprint present OR --fingerprint-profile decoding to a non-empty capture,
resolved once per process. Modes: no persona = host values everywhere; seed = full persona plus
farble; profile = full persona from the capture over the seed-0 base, no farble. Farble/noise gates
(farble seed, canvas/WebGL readback, audio perturbation, the pro coalesced-pointer sampler) stay on
the seed. A capture's uaFullVersion is honoured only within the engine major. A touch-capable
desktop persona exposes the coarse pointer bit next to the fine one (any-pointer:coarse), the
shape a real touch laptop has.

Measured (Windows, headed, loopback page): profile="auto" now serves the donor's screen, DPR,
voices, UA-CH version, heap limit and GPU string together; seed B's page reports the persona's
151.0.7922.108 where the old draw gave entry 0; bare and light_stealth unchanged versus r18.

