+// clearcote: THE persona-activation predicate. True when this launch carries a
+// persona -- a seed (--fingerprint) or an imported capture (--fingerprint-profile
+// whose payload decodes to a non-empty capture) -- and every surface that can
+// serve a persona value (screen, work area, DPR, pointer/touch, cores, memory,
+// heap limit, audio rate/latency, voices, fonts, UA-CH version, window sizing)
+// consults it through this ONE function.
+//
+// Launch modes, so the split is explicit rather than per patch:
+//   no persona          neither switch: every surface serves the HOST value
+//                       (plus any explicit --fingerprint-<field> override).
+//   seeded              --fingerprint=<seed>: full persona from the seed; the
+//                       seed also keys the canvas/WebGL/audio farble.
+//   imported profile    --fingerprint-profile=<capture>: full persona = the
+//                       capture's fields over the seed-0 base; NO farble seed.
+//                       A payload that does not decode activates nothing.
+//   platform / brand    --fingerprint-platform / --fingerprint-brand alone do
+//                       NOT activate a persona; they only shape the UA family.
+//
+// Before this predicate the gates were per patch: most tested the seed only, so
+// an imported profile applied to fonts and WebGL strings but not to screen, DPR,
+// pointer, cores, memory or voices; and cores, heap limit and audio latency read
+// the persona in EVERY mode, so a bare launch claimed a persona core count over
+// host hardware everywhere else (file 70).
+//
+// Farble/noise gates (farble_seed.cc, the canvas/WebGL readback and audio
+// perturbation paths, the pro coalesced-pointer sampler) deliberately stay on
+// --fingerprint: they need a seed, not a persona.
+COMPONENT_EXPORT(UNGOOGLED) bool PersonaActive();
+
